description: Language and copy conventions for product vs code
---

# Language conventions

- **Code** (identifiers, types, API field names in contracts): English.
- **User-facing product copy** (QQ replies, Web UI, user error messages): zh/en via i18n keys; do not hardcode monolingual long strings in feature code.
- **Engineering docs** in-repo: Chinese or short bilingual is fine.
- **Comments**: function TSDoc in English with full `@param`/`@returns`; inline Chinese or English; ≥80% comment-required coverage; never paste agent chat (see `commit-and-comments` / CODING_STANDARDS).
- Brand string in UI: **Lanius**; never misspell as Lanuis.
- Realm labels: 国际服 / International; 国服 reserved for later — MVP UI may hide or show "coming soon".
